Falsifies `sealed_pair::verification::a_table_line_vouches_for_an_entry_exactly_when_the_digests_are_equal`.

The defect: the comparison looks only at the first byte of the two digests. An entry whose bytes
changed but whose hash still starts with the table's first byte reads as described by the table, and
the check calls a tampered archive consistent. Every test that changes an entry changes a hash whose
first byte differs too, so they still pass.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!` on `Changed`, with two digests that share a first byte.

diff --git a/crates/sealed_pair/src/lib.rs b/crates/sealed_pair/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/sealed_pair/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/sealed_pair/src/lib.rs
@@ -514,7 +514,7 @@
 ) -> Option<TableDisagreement> {
     match listed.iter().find(|(n, _)| *n == name) {
         None => Some(TableDisagreement::Unlisted(name.to_string())),
-        Some((_, want)) if *want != have => Some(TableDisagreement::Changed(name.to_string())),
+        Some((_, want)) if want[0] != have[0] => Some(TableDisagreement::Changed(name.to_string())),
         Some(_) => None,
     }
 }
